WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.450
So, I just wanted us
all to kind of connect,

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.370
and get on the same page in terms of

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.500
what the communication plan is for

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.270
when we announce Fusion Arena.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.120
But, I figure before we dive into this,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.513
we could watch the final video.

00:00:14.648 --> 00:00:17.457
Wow.

00:00:17.457 --> 00:00:18.872
Oh, this is so hype.

00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:22.120
Oh, that's straight to
the top of the Reddit.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.110
This is going to be the first stadium,

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.070
built just for video games
in the United States.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.750
And, they're building it in Philadelphia,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.153
a town known for its,
well, passionate fans.

00:00:31.153 --> 00:00:32.710
Eagles!

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.490
In fact, here is where the Eagles play,

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.450
and that's the Phillies Stadium.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.380
The Fusion Arena, as it'll be called,

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.213
will be right in the center
of Philadelphia sports.

00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:43.370
This is the story of how Comcast,

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.950
is building on the passion
of Philadelphia sports fans,

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.795
to create a global eSports juggernaut.

00:00:48.795 --> 00:00:50.900
Leading that endeavor,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.366
is this man, Tucker Roberts.

00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:53.960
And, it's worth noting that

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.930
he's not just any
casually-dressed executive.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.780
He also happens to be
the son of Comcast CEO,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.850
Brian Roberts, and
grandson of Ralph Roberts,

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.400
the Co-Founder of the company,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.390
which is now worth nearly $200 billion.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.810
I've been a gamer all my life,

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.930
much to the chagrin of
my parents and my grades.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.180
But when online gaming started,

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.900
that really was a game changer for me,

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.800
in terms of connecting
people to other people,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.510
I thought was so fascinating,

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.770
and now everybody plays
video games, today,

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:23.840
in every single country.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.620
And so, when you think about

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.676
how big is that business opportunity,

00:01:27.676 --> 00:01:30.900
it could be the biggest
one of all of them.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.670
Comcast is joining a growing field

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.660
of media and sports titans
that are investing in eSports,

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:38.990
including Michael Jordan, Dallas
Cowboys owner, Jerry Jones,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.330
and Atlanta's Cox Communications.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.470
But, the company isn't new
to sports entertainment.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.290
The US' largest cable provider

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.760
has invested heavily in
sports throughout the years.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.990
Just look at their flagship
market of Philadelphia,

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.300
where it's nearly impossible
to separate Comcast

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.680
from the local sports teams.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.070
Comcast owns broadcasting rights

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.690
to nearly all Phillies,
Sixers, and Flyers games,

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.550
and even has full ownership of the Flyers

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.530
and their stadium, the Wells Fargo Center.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.290
Traditional sports, or sports in general,

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.520
is the DVR proof event of our time,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.080
and it always kind of will
stand the test of time.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.450
This is Joe Marsh.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.310
for this new division of
Comcast, and believes esports

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.370
can be a large part of
the company's business.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.640
In terms of what gaming could be

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.133
for Comcast-Spectacor and the company,

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.570
I really think it could be
a billion dollar business.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.670
To put that in perspective,

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.930
after 50 years, their
ice hockey franchise,

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:27.090
the Flyers, have yet to hit a valuation

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.210
over a billion dollars.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.800
Comcast's investment in
esports began in 2017,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.720
when they purchased the
Overwatch League franchise

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.430
for $20 million,
borrowing the color scheme

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.360
of the Flyers, they named the team Fusion,

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.210
and began to try to build a fan base.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.820
We were starting as a non endemic team,

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.179
with zero followers, so
how do you build a fan base

00:02:45.179 --> 00:02:48.300
from thin air, without
making it inauthentic?

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.606
'Cause you can buy fans,

00:02:49.606 --> 00:02:52.283
but that's not how we
were gonna build our team.

00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:54.690
Most of the players to
the Fusion live here

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.260
in this large suburban
home, outside of LA,

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.140
decked out with Overwatch
imagery, gaming PCs,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.940
and even a personal chef.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.630
The biggest thing I think we've done,

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.477
especially around our content is that,

00:03:05.477 --> 00:03:08.240
the branding and the
imagery you see of our team,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.340
is very Philly-centric.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.457
It's very Philly-based.

00:03:10.457 --> 00:03:11.881
Even though the team

00:03:11.881 --> 00:03:13.200
is made of mostly international players,

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.950
the Fusion's YouTube channel
is filled with videos

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.710
of players wearing
Philadelphia team shirts,

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:22.700
opening care packages of
Tastykake and WAWA Coffee.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.963
And, yes, even Gritty makes an appearance.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.410
But, all of this content
isn't about the game.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.970
It's about the players themselves.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.830
esports fans want to see
everything our guys do.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.283
What they ate for breakfast,

00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:36.130
Chef Heidi's posting that on Twitter.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:36.980
If they hit the gym,

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.440
or played around with the soccer net,

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.760
the difference of esports
and regular sports is,

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.500
you can see yourself
in the Fusion players.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.890
We wanna give you that access to feel like

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.170
you're part of the team
because, one day you could be.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.440
And that's the dream that
we're trying to help foster.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.531
What also helped their
popularity, was winning.

00:03:55.531 --> 00:03:57.570
The Fusion is going to the Grand Finals!

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.160
The Fusion became that underdog team,

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.310
that worked its way from
the bottom of the playoffs,

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.690
all the way to the finals.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.791
And even though the team lost
to the London-based franchise,

00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:07.560
their fans were there to support them.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.300
15,000 people or so, there at the finals,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.100
cheering as the Fusion come out.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.130
And, my family got to be there with me,

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.470
which was really special.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.277
It was a surreal experience for me to go,

00:04:19.277 --> 00:04:24.057
"Wow, it went from fights about the Wi-Fi

00:04:24.057 --> 00:04:27.247
"at 2 a.m when I was in middle school to

00:04:27.247 --> 00:04:30.360
"here I am and they're
all cheering for my team."

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.140
There's a chance Tucker
succeeds his father,

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.760
at the top of Comcast, someday,

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.470
much as Brian took over
from his dad 17 years ago.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.470
But, that's getting ahead of things.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.620
There are more pressing concerns.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.370
While Overwatch enjoyed initial success

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.100
with its release in 2016,

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.930
its average views on Twitch
have decreased over time.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.830
And, when we visited a
regular season match at,

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.790
Blizzard arena in Burbank, California.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.560
The 530 seat theater
was less than half full

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.760
on a Friday night.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.072
But, Tucker is still betting
on the side of eSports,

00:04:57.072 --> 00:04:58.500
and nowhere is that more apparent,

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.630
than the $50 million
investment in the Fusion Arena,

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.910
set to break ground in
the next few months.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.920
The Fusion Arena is going
to be the first of its kind.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.210
It's gonna be, in my opinion,

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.840
the best arena for
eSports in North America.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.990
It'll be a 3500 capacity
purpose-built venue.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:17.823
It's gonna be kind of like an EDM concert,

00:05:17.823 --> 00:05:20.080
but you're gonna be watching the Fusion.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.920
While the Fusion Arena bears the name

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.050
of their Overwatch team,
it serves a purpose

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.810
beyond just that game.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.610
For Comcast, it's a longterm play,

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.530
to reach a global audience.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.540
There's global market that will benefit

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.050
from this gaming hub being
built in Philadelphia.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:37.560
It's an attractive
place for a lot of games

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.740
to have their events.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.710
You're going to be able to get viewership

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.640
in the West Coast, but also in Europe,

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:43.900
and you're going to be able to do it

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:44.930
at a fraction of the cost

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.890
of some of the other
cities on the East Coast.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.560
And, after a recent
venture with SK Telecom,

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.370
South Korea's largest wireless carrier,

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.423
and owner of a wildly
successful eSports team...

00:05:54.423 --> 00:05:56.863
The undisputed, best team in the world,

00:05:56.863 --> 00:05:58.360
the SK Team reign continues...

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.230
Comcast hopes to diversify their foothold

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:01.310
in multiple games.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.870
The new entity, T1
Entertainment and Sports,

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.480
expands their game portfolio

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.110
into some of the most
popular esports franchises,

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.620
League of Legends,
Hearthstone, PUBG, and more.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.070
Really, what we're gonna
do there is enhance

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.440
everything that our South
Korean counterparts have done,

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.523
and now the plan is to take that model,

00:06:19.523 --> 00:06:21.006
and go global with it.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.330
But for now, the Fusion Arena

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.530
is still just a parking lot,

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.370
across the street from the Eagles Stadium.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.170
A new report puts global esports revenue

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.000
at just over $1 billion
dollars, this year.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.620
In comparison, global revenue

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.400
for the traditional leagues and teams,

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.150
is around $100 billion.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:37.600
And if you include all the
industry around the sports,

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.213
revenue is estimated to be $1 trillion.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.520
So, if Tucker wants to make his mark

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.800
on his family's business
with a global esports empire,

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:48.000
one that could even rival their
traditional sports empire,

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.400
it's gonna take time.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.430
And, for it to work, a whole
new community of sports fans,

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.810
will need to emerge.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:57.430
To build a gaming arena
in South Philadelphia,

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.770
kind of legitimizes what we're doing.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:00.907
Like, "Look, we're right in the heart

00:07:00.907 --> 00:07:02.660
"of South Philadelphia Sports Complex."

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.400
I'm a huge Philly Sports fan,

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.500
so it's really a dream come
true to work on something

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.710
that represents the city.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.670
There's such a strong community
within our Fusion Discord.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:14.300
They're coming up with
sometimes even without us,

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.337
just saying, "Hey, who
wants to meet up over here,

00:07:16.337 --> 00:07:18.740
"and play some games, or go
to this movie, together?"

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:22.470
And so, the fact that we
fostered that in any small way,

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:25.933
is really awesome to see, and
makes everything worth it.

